    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We know that at the point of intersection, the y-coordinates of both lines are equal to 10, and the x-coordinates are 6. Thus, we can set the equations equal to each other and solve for one of the variables to get the value of m.\n\nSimplifying the equations yields:\n\\begin{align*}\n10 &= 6m + 4 \\\\\n6 &= 3m + b\n\\end{align*}\n\nSolving these simultaneous equations, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\nb &= 6 - 3m \\\\\n10 &= 6m + 4 \\\\\n10 - 4 &= 6m \\\\\n2 &= 6m \\\\\n\\frac{2}{6} &= m \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3} &= m\\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nPlugging in the value of m into the second equation yields:\n\\begin{align*}\n10 &= 6\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) + b \\\\\n10 &= 2 + b\n\\end{align*}\n\n$10 - 2 = b$ thus $b = 8$. Summing $b$ and $m$, we get:\n\\[\nb + m = 8 + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{24+1}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{25}{3}}\n\\]\nThe answer is: \\frac{25}{3}",
